  "articleBody": "While some home projects are great for DIY, installing door casings can sometimes be trickier than it looks, especially if you want a truly polished finish. Here's when bringing in a professional really makes sense:\n* **Walls or jambs are out of square:** If your walls aren't perfectly straight or your door jambs aren't perfectly plumb, getting that casing to look right is a serious challenge. Pros have the experience and tools to compensate for these imperfections, making it look seamless. \n* **Uneven openings:** Not all door openings are created equal! If yours is a bit wonky, a professional can custom-fit the casing so it looks intentional and clean, not crooked.\n* **Matching existing millwork:** Trying to perfectly match new casing to existing trim in other parts of your home takes a keen eye and skill. A pro can ensure consistency in style and finish.\n* **Precise trim removal and finish restoration:** If you're replacing old casing and need to carefully remove it without damaging surrounding surfaces, or if the job involves intricate finish work like staining or painting, an expert will deliver a much cleaner result. \n* **Complex styles or materials:** If you've chosen intricate, delicate, or expensive casing materials, you want someone with experience handling them to avoid costly mistakes. \nFor detailed, high-quality work that truly enhances your home, consider reaching out to HH Remodeling LLC. We handle these challenges daily for homeowners in Aurora, Commerce City, and many other Denver-area communities.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}